{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "x-touch-compact-mc",
  "name": "Behringer X-Touch Compact (MC Mode)",
  "notes": "Behringer X-Touch Compact in Mackie Control (MC) mode - hold the bottom-left button (1) while powering on, release after the unit blinks twice, then the MC LED lights. HARDWARE-VERIFIED 2026-07-27 by live MIDI capture against a real unit (input side): faders send 14-bit pitchbend on channels 1-8 (main = 9) and are motorized; the 8 top encoders send relative MC deltas on CC 16-23 (1..8 = CW, 65..72 = CCW) with push notes 32-39 and LED rings on CC 48-55 (values 32 = off .. 43 = full); button rows send notes 8-15 / 16-23 / 24-31 (MC Solo/Mute/Select), the buttons under the faders notes 0-7 (MC Rec), the main fader button note 50 (MC Flip). MC-mode quirks, all confirmed on hardware: side encoders 9-14 transmit NOTHING when turned - only their push sends (MC V-Pot assign notes 40-45); side encoders 15/16 are the opposite - the push is silent and each rotation detent fires a note press (15: 46 CCW / 47 CW, 16: 48 CCW / 49 CW, MC fader-bank/channel). Each is modeled as a note-pair ENCODER: the clockwise note is the control's own address, the counter-clockwise note is encoding.decrementNote - one detent press = +/-1. SIDE ENCODER LED RINGS (9-16) ARE NOT CONTROLLABLE IN MC MODE - hardware-verified 2026-08-01: the unit ignores every candidate RX scheme for them (standard-mode 'LED ring change' CC 18-25, 'LED ring remote' CC 34-41, and a hypothetical MC V-Pot continuation CC 56-63, each tried on channels 1+2 with values 6/13/27/43/127), while the 8 top rings on CC 48-55 respond normally. So knob-9..14 pushes carry a plain LED capability at most and knob-15/16 declare no ledRing; if ring feedback on the side encoders matters, use the standard-mode board (x-touch-compact-relative) instead. Layer A/B send notes 84/85 (no hardware layer switching in MC mode). The 6 side buttons are the MC transport block: 91/92/86/95/93/94 in reading order. Fader touch notes 104-112 are deliberately not declared (ignored). LED/motor feedback follows the MC standard: echo the control's own note/pitchbend/ring CC back.",
  "manufacturer": "Behringer",
  "mode": "mc",
  "setupInstructions": "1. Switch the unit off.\n2. Hold the bottom-left button (1).\n3. Turn the device on and still hold the button pressed.\n4. The device will blink two times.\n5. Release the button, the MC LED should now light up.",
